    "**Discussion (fill in from your results above):**\n",
    "- *Best optimizer / learning rate and why.* Adam adapts a separate step size per weight, so it is usually the least sensitive to the learning rate. With batch normalisation, SGD + Momentum at a fairly high learning rate is often just as good.\n",
    "- *Learning rate.* Too large → loss jumps around; too small (especially plain SGD at 0.0005) → still improving when the epoch budget runs out.\n",
    "- *Momentum.* Averages past gradients, so it moves faster along consistent directions and damps zig-zagging – compare SGD and SGD + Momentum at the same learning rate."
   ]
